What is type safety in api testing?
it ensure that the data sent to and received from an API matches the exact data type expected (like a number, text, or a date etc.,,). 
It acts as a safety net that catches data errors automatically before they can break our application.
Advantages:
----------------
• Prevents Silly Mistakes: If a developer accidentally changes an API field from a number (100) to text ("100"), a type-safe test will instantly flag it.
• Auto-Complete Support: Because the testing tool knows exactly what data types to expect, it can suggest field names to you while you write your tests.
• Early Warnings: It catches bugs while you are writing the code, rather than waiting for the API to run and crash.

we can achive type safety by creating an interface of our request body values.

